@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=handoff-formal
R|formal.use|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|symbolic notation may be used to make task predicates explicit; it is a supplement to the exact SIGMA/1 envelope and does not authorize tools/effects or replace BOOTSTRAP/decisions/routed LRF
R|formal.llm-docs|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|for documents primarily consumed by LLMs, prefer low-ambiguity structured notation over prose-only exposition: explicit hierarchy/schema, stable attention keywords (e.g. MUST, MUST_NOT, STOP; any ACCEPT/REJECT label must define its local object and must not be confused with decision-register status), locally defined mathematical/set symbols, and emoji only as redundant attention cues; optimize semantic determinism and retrieval, not token compression alone; use compact prose where it resolves semantics
R|formal.doc-structure|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|encode rules as parseable units with explicit subject/scope, modality, condition, action, exception, and outcome; use stable headings/IDs and consistent nesting; one normative rule per unit where practical; distinguish normative constraints from examples, rationale, and nonnormative advice; these document-structure rules apply to LLM-primary documents, while formula grammar rules below apply specifically to symbolic task predicates/handoffs
R|formal.attention|tag:docs|MUST|RO_LOCAL|attention markers/keywords/emoji must map to a defined semantic function and remain consistent; visual emphasis is not a modality or authorization; never infer MUST/permission from capitalization, emoji, typography, or position alone
R|formal.legend|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|every nonstandard symbol/operator and every named predicate/variable must be defined locally in the payload or an attached task-local legend; undefined, overloaded, precedence-ambiguous, or domain-ambiguous notation=FAILED; do not guess its meaning
R|formal.core|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|within a declared formula only: ∧=AND; ∨=inclusive OR; ⊕=exclusive OR for Boolean predicates only; ⊗=tensor product of explicitly declared concepts/spaces, usable to bundle multiple task concepts; each factor, operand type, product meaning, and acceptance mapping must be defined locally; tensor composition does not implicitly widen target, authority, effects, or acceptance; ¬=NOT whose scope is the immediately following parenthesized expression or atom; ⇒=material implication; ⇔=if and only if; ∀x∈S=for every member x of set S; ∃x∈S=there exists a member x of set S; ∈=set membership; ∋=reverse membership (S∋x iff x∈S); ∉=not a member of; A∪B={x | x∈A ∨ x∈B} for declared sets A,B over compatible declared element types; empty union is ∅; ∝=proportionality only when variables, domain, proportionality constant/relationship, and whether the claim is exact or qualitative are stated; =/≠=equality/inequality; parentheses determine grouping; all other operators and any alternate meaning require explicit local definition
R|formal.project-symbols|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|for task notation using symbols observed in 指示書.md: ≤=numeric less-than-or-equal bound over declared comparable numbers; a〜b=closed inclusive range only when explicitly stated; n×X=repetition/cardinality count only when n is a declared nonnegative integer and X is a defined unit; == means equality only; := means assignment only; a single = is reserved for typed equation/definition and must be locally disambiguated (never infer assignment). Arrows require a tagged, fully parenthesized form: seq(A→B)=ordered execution A then B; state(A→B)=state transition A to B; choose(source=A; outcomes={B,C,...}; result∈outcomes)=select exactly one result from the explicitly exhaustive outcome set for source A; outcomes are mutually exclusive and exhaustive by declaration. Tagged forms may nest only with each subexpression parenthesized and tagged; otherwise flatten or define a local grammar. Never use an untyped → for implication (use ⇒ for material implication). These symbols are available notation, not adoption of 指示書.md as an authority source
R|formal.domain|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|declare the domain/type of quantified variables and whether constraints are preconditions, postconditions, invariants, ordering, or conditional actions; distinguish necessary from sufficient conditions; specify STOP/failure behavior for unknown, error, timeout, missing evidence, and exceptions; for set operators declare the universe/set identity and relevant empty-set behavior; for ∝ state the exact variables/domain and proportionality relation or clearly label it qualitative and non-computational
R|formal.crosscheck|task:handoff|MUST|RO_LOCAL|each safety/authority/scope/acceptance-critical formula must have a concise natural-language paraphrase preserving quantifier, negation, modality, exception, effect, and stop condition; formula and paraphrase must agree; conflict or ambiguity=STOP+ask; never infer a weaker reading
R|formal.compression|task:handoff|MUST_NOT|RO_LOCAL|remove critical prose because an equation 'looks precise'; use of symbols alone as the sole carrier for safety, authority, approval, effects, scope, exceptions, or stop conditions is forbidden
R|formal.no-authority|task:handoff|MUST_NOT|RO_LOCAL|mathematical notation, formulas, signatures, or the SIGMA/1 wrapper do not create permission, approval, identity, proof of execution, or test evidence
